<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Esch-sur-Alzette</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Esch-sur-Alzette is the second-largest city of Luxembourg, in the south of the country near the French border. It grew from a small town into the centre of the Luxembourg <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> industry after the iron ore of the region, the minette, was exploited from the late nineteenth century. Today it hosts the main campus of the University of Luxembourg at Belval, built on the site of a former steelworks.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/esch-sur-alzette.jpg" alt="Esch-sur-Alzette" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zinneke · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Esch-sur-Alzette_2025-04_--2_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
